{
  "_comment": "WTF-520: searches in a repeating group's cells, read for every cell together (one query per cell round, never one per cell; two keys: the customer and its owner). A reusable tag rendered only in the cells searches with a text comparison no batch can key: that search alone is not loaded, the tag is still rendered per cell. A second tag with the same search is also rendered once, outside the list: there the search loads, and its instances in the cells are not rendered per cell. Customers and their orders, all data invented; test/support/target/phoenix/cell_searches_behavior.exs counts the queries.",
  "_id": "cell-searches-fixture",
